#Terminal Commands-  
#git add = Stage files for your next commit.
#. = Include files in the current folder and its subfolders, except ignored files.
#git commit — Saves a snapshot of your staged project files in Git's history.
#-m — Allows you to include a short message.

#Think of a commit as a checkpoint in your project's history. If you make changes later, Git helps you compare them with earlier versions.

#git remote → Manage connections to remote repositories.
add → Add a new connection.
origin → The name we give our GitHub repository.
URL → The address of your repository on GitHub.

#git branch → Manages branches
-M → Renames your current branch.
main → The name of your primary development branch.